Section 1: Explanation — What is Prompt Engineering?
What it is
Prompt Engineering is the art of communicating clearly and strategically with an AI like Claude to get the most accurate, useful, and relevant response. Think of it as learning how to ask the right question, the right way.
Just like how you'd give a new employee clear instructions rather than vague ones, AI needs specific, well-structured input to deliver quality output.
Why it matters
AI tools are only as powerful as the instructions you give them. A poorly written prompt produces a generic, unhelpful response. A well-engineered prompt produces results that feel like they were created by an expert. The difference isn't the AI — it's you, the prompter. This is now a genuine career skill in the AI era.

Section 2: Weak vs. Improved Prompt Example
PromptOutput
❌ Weak"Write me something about marketing.
"A vague, generic 3-paragraph essay with no direction or usefulness
✅ Engineered"Write a 200-word Instagram caption for a Gen-Z skincare brand. Use a friendly, relatable tone. 
End with a call-to-action encouraging followers to comment their skin type."A targeted, on-brand caption — ready to publish, right length, right tone
The difference? Context + Audience + Format + Goal. These four elements transform any prompt.

Section 3: Three Practical Benefits
1. Saves time — Well-structured prompts reduce back-and-forth iterations. You get what you need on the first or second try instead of the seventh.
2. Better accuracy — When you specify role, format, and purpose, the AI understands your intent and delivers with far greater precision.
3. Unlocks creativity — A good prompt is a creative briefing. It lets the AI act as a skilled collaborator rather than a generic text generator.
